# AI Features Documentation Rule

**AI features are currently switched OFF for every user** and cannot be enabled at runtime. The
single switch is `AI_FEATURES_ENABLED` in `libs/shared/ai-client/src/lib/ai-feature-flag.service.ts`.
No feature code was removed, so everything below still describes what is in the tree — but do not
assume any of it is reachable, and do not "fix" the flag because a feature looks broken.
See `AGENTS/10-ai-features.md` for what the kill switch covers.

AI features are served by Nuxeo Automation operations (`AI.*`) from a **separate** marketplace
package repository. This repo contains only the Angular client (`libs/shared/ai-client`).

The application includes the following AI features:

1. **Natural Language Search** — Convert plain English to NXQL queries (Search page + Admin NXQL page)
2. **Document Summarization** — AI-generated summary with key points (Document Detail > AI Insights tab)
3. **AI Tag Suggestions** — Recommend tags with confidence scores, one-click apply (Document Detail > AI Insights tab)
4. **Document Classification** — Suggest description, nature, subjects, workflow (Document Detail > AI Insights tab)
5. **Similar Documents** — Find related documents via embeddings + cosine similarity (Document Detail > AI Insights tab)
6. **AI Chat Assistant** — RAG-powered conversational assistant with context awareness (App header drawer)
7. **Dashboard AI Insights** — Personalized actionable insights based on tasks and activity (Dashboard widget)
8. **Audit Anomaly Detection** — AI analysis of audit events for security anomalies (Admin > Analytics tab)
9. **Comment Sentiment Analysis** — Classify comment sentiment and summarize threads (API ready)
10. **Natural Language Permission Queries** — Answer "who can access what" questions via ACL analysis (API ready)

When modifying any AI-related code (Angular AI components, AI client services), you MUST also update `docs/ai-features.md` to reflect the changes.

Specifically:
- If you add, remove, or rename an automation operation call, update the corresponding feature section and the Project Structure listing.
- If you change request/response shapes, update the API examples in the relevant feature section.
- If you add a new AI feature, add a new numbered section following the existing format (heading, location, description, table of files, API example).
- If you change which OpenAI model a feature uses, update the Models Used table.
- If you add new environment variables, update the Environment Variables table.
- If you modify the project structure (new files/folders), update the Project Structure tree.
